From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:21:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] soc: sdp: add Micom message box, Micom protocol core and remote control

Build 070 (IR, P1): Linux 6.6 port of Samsung's GPL Micom stack from the
20_DTV_NikeL package for the Q60T (Nike-L):

- drivers/soc/sdp/sdp-msgbox.c: CPU<->Micom hardware mailbox
  ("samsung,sdp-messagebox"), from linux-4.1.10/drivers/mailbox/
  sdp_micom_msgbox.c
- drivers/soc/sdp/sdp-micom.c: Micom packet protocol and client dispatch
  ("samsung,tztv-micom"), from tztv-micom/sdp_micom_messagebox.c
- drivers/media/rc/sdp-micom-rc.c: rc-core scancode device with Samsung's
  key map, from tztv-micom/rc-wt61p807.c and keymap-rc-wt61p807.c

The Micom decodes the IR remote and the panel keys itself; this is the
path Samsung's own kernel uses for the remote. DT: message box and Micom
nodes from the firmware DT (status disabled); soc node renamed soc@0
(dtc W=1 unit_address_vs_reg). Compile-only: nothing was run on a TV.
---
